#. Tag: title
#: tabstops.docbook:11
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using Tab Stops"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: tabstops.docbook:12 tabstops.docbook:63 tabstops.docbook:155
#: tabstops.docbook:237 tabstops.docbook:238 tabstops.docbook:313
#, no-c-format
msgid "tab stops"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: tabstops.docbook:12
#, no-c-format
msgid "using"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: tabstops.docbook:13
#, no-c-format
msgid "paragraph"
msgstr "paragraf"

#. Tag: secondary
#: tabstops.docbook:13
#, no-c-format
msgid "setting tab stops"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tabstops.docbook:15
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Tab stops are a (very useful) holdover from the days of typewriters. They "
"allow you to align text into columns quickly and easily."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tabstops.docbook:19
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When a tab stop is in place, you can immediately jump to a horizontal "
"position on the page by pressing the <keycap>Tab</keycap> key. Tab stops are "
"most commonly used to align columns in a table, or to automatically indent "
"paragraphs."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tabstops.docbook:24
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Tab stops are part of the properties of a paragraph. Each paragraph keeps "
"track of its own set of tab stops. To view the tab stops of a particular "
"paragraph, place the mouse pointer within a paragraph, click once, and check "
"the top ruler. The tab stops are marked as symbols in black."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tabstops.docbook:30
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kword; recognizes 4 types of tab stops. Each of these types has a "
"corresponding symbol to help you identify the type in the ruler."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: tabstops.docbook:36
#, no-c-format
msgid "Type"
msgstr "Tipe"

#. Tag: entry
#: tabstops.docbook:36
#, no-c-format
msgid "Example"
msgstr "Exemple"

#. Tag: entry
#: tabstops.docbook:36
#, no-c-format
msgid "Symbol"
msgstr "Simbòl"

#. Tag: entry
#: tabstops.docbook:36
#, no-c-format
msgid "Description"
msgstr "Descripcion"

#. Tag: entry
#: tabstops.docbook:39
#, no-c-format
msgid "Right Tab Stop"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: tabstops.docbook:42
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"With a right tab stop, the right edge of the next set of words is aligned at "
"the tab stop."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: tabstops.docbook:44
#, no-c-format
msgid "Center Tab Stop"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: tabstops.docbook:47
#, no-c-format
msgid "With a center tab stop, the text is centered at the tab stop."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: tabstops.docbook:49
#, no-c-format
msgid "Left Tab Stop"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: tabstops.docbook:52
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"With a left tab stop, the left edge of the next set of words is aligned at "
"the tab stop."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: tabstops.docbook:54
#, no-c-format
msgid "Decimal Tab Stop"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: tabstops.docbook:57
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"With a decimal tab stop, the decimal points of the text are aligned at the "
"tab stop."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: tabstops.docbook:62
#, no-c-format
msgid "Setting Tab Stops"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: tabstops.docbook:63
#, no-c-format
msgid "setting a new tab stop"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tabstops.docbook:65
#, no-c-format
msgid "Tab stops can be set one of two ways:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: link
#: tabstops.docbook:69 tabstops.docbook:161 tabstops.docbook:246
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using the rulers of &kword;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: link
#: tabstops.docbook:73 tabstops.docbook:165 tabstops.docbook:250
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using a specialized dialog panel."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: tabstops.docbook:79 tabstops.docbook:171 tabstops.docbook:256
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using the Ruler"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tabstops.docbook:81
#, no-c-format
msgid "You can use the top ruler of &kword; to interactively insert tab stops."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tabstops.docbook:84
#, no-c-format
msgid "First, you should select the type of tab stop you want to use."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tabstops.docbook:87
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Place the mouse cursor over the current tab character (located directly to "
"the left of the top ruler). Click once with the &RMB;. A small popup menu "
"will appear. You can select the tab stop you want from the sub menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tabstops.docbook:93
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can also use the left mouse button to cycle through the different types "
"of tab stops."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tabstops.docbook:96
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click once on the current tab character, and the tab stop changes from left "
"tab stop, to center tab stop. If you continue to click with the left mouse "
"button, you will change to right tab stop, then to decimal tab stop, then "
"back to left tab stop."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tabstops.docbook:103
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Once you have the correct type of tab stop, you can simply place the mouse "
"pointer on the top ruler bar at the desired position, and click once with "
"the &LMB;. This will place a tab stop at that position."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: tabstops.docbook:111 tabstops.docbook:194 tabstops.docbook:272
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using the Dialog Box"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tabstops.docbook:113
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The fastest way to get to the tab stop dialog panel, is to select "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Format</guimenu><guimenuitem>Paragraph...</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the menubar or type <keycombo action=\"simul"
"\">&Ctrl;&Alt;<keycap>P</keycap></keycombo>. This will bring up a dialog box "
"with 5 tabs. Click on the tab labeled <guilabel>Tabulators</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tabstops.docbook:126
#, no-c-format
msgid "You can now add tab stops by:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tabstops.docbook:130
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click the <guibutton>New</guibutton> button at the bottom of the list of tab "
"stops."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tabstops.docbook:133 tabstops.docbook:218
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Type the horizontal location of the tab stop in the space labeled "
"<guilabel>Position</guilabel>. The units used and the current frame width "
"are listed below the text box."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tabstops.docbook:138
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select the type of tab stop from the list of radio buttons labeled "
"<guilabel>Alignment</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tabstops.docbook:141
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Determine what you want to fill the empty space to the tab stop with. In "
"most cases this should be left as <guilabel>Blank</guilabel>. For "
"information on other options in this section, see <link linkend=\"tab-fill"
"\">Tab filling</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tabstops.docbook:147
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can now add another tab stop. When you are done adding tab stops, you "
"can click <guibutton>OK</guibutton> to finish."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: tabstops.docbook:154
#, no-c-format
msgid "Moving Tab Stops"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: tabstops.docbook:155
#, no-c-format
msgid "moving"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tabstops.docbook:157
#, no-c-format
msgid "Tab stops can be moved one of two ways:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tabstops.docbook:175
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To move a tab stop with the ruler, place the mouse over the desired tab "
"stop. The mouse pointer will change to a double arrow."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tabstops.docbook:181
#, no-c-format
msgid "Click and hold down the &LMB;. Drag the tab stop to its new location"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tabstops.docbook:186
#, no-c-format
msgid "When the tab stop is where you want it, release the mouse button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tabstops.docbook:196 tabstops.docbook:274
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select <menuchoice><guimenu>Format</guimenu><guimenuitem>Paragraph...</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the menubar or type <keycombo action=\"simul"
"\">&Ctrl;&Alt;<keycap>P</keycap></keycombo>. This will bring up a dialog box "
"with 5 tabs."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tabstops.docbook:200 tabstops.docbook:278
#, no-c-format
msgid "Click on the tab labeled <guilabel>Tabulators</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tabstops.docbook:202 tabstops.docbook:280
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A very fast way to edit existing tab stops is to simply double click on the "
"tab stop you want to edit in the top ruler of &kword;. This will also bring "
"up the <guilabel>Tabulators</guilabel> dialog box with the desired tab stop "
"already selected."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tabstops.docbook:214
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click on the tab stop you want moved. The list of all tab stops is in the "
"box on the left side of the dialog panel."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tabstops.docbook:224
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you need to make changes, select the type of tab stop from the list "
"labeled <guilabel>Alignment</guilabel> or change the white space character "
"under <guilabel>Tab Leader</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tabstops.docbook:229
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click <guibutton>OK</guibutton> when you are done moving all tab stops "
"around."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: tabstops.docbook:236
#, no-c-format
msgid "Removing Tab Stops"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: tabstops.docbook:237
#, no-c-format
msgid "removing"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: tabstops.docbook:238
#, no-c-format
msgid "deleting"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tabstops.docbook:240
#, no-c-format
msgid "Tab stops can be removed one of two ways:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tabstops.docbook:260
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To delete a tab stop with the ruler, place the mouse over the desired tab "
"stop. The mouse pointer will change to a double arrow."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tabstops.docbook:265
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click and hold down the &RMB; on the mouse. A popup menu will appear. Select "
"<guimenuitem>Remove Tabulator</guimenuitem>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tabstops.docbook:293
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click on the tab stop you want removed. The list of all tab stops is in the "
"box on the left side of the dialog panel"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tabstops.docbook:297
#, no-c-format
msgid "Click the <guibutton>Delete</guibutton> button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tabstops.docbook:301
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can delete all tab stops at once by clicking <guibutton>Delete All</"
"guibutton>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tabstops.docbook:302
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kword; will not prompt you prior to deleting all tabs, so make sure that is "
"your intention prior to selecting the <guibutton>Delete All</guibutton> "
"button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tabstops.docbook:306
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you are done deleting tab stops, you can click <guibutton>OK</"
"guibutton> to finish."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: tabstops.docbook:312
#, no-c-format
msgid "Tab filling"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: tabstops.docbook:313
#, no-c-format
msgid "tab filling"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tabstops.docbook:315
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By default, &kword; uses the standard tab function that you are familiar "
"with when using a typewriter or most wordprocessing programs. You can, "
"however, have &kword; insert dots or lines to fill the tab space."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tabstops.docbook:317
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To change the way the tab fills work in &kword; you change the combo box "
"labeled <guilabel>Filling:</guilabel>. This combo box gives you many "
"different line styles to choose from."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tabstops.docbook:319
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can change the thickness of the lines by using the <guilabel>Width:</"
"guilabel> spin box."
msgstr ""
